# Epitaxial Crystal Growth Simulation

Monte Carlo simulation of epitaxial crystal growth using Solid-on-Solid and Zinc Blende models implemented in Python. This project explores the simulation of Molecular Beam Epitaxy (MBE) processes and evaluates the impact of parallel computing techniques on computational performance.

> **Status:** Active academic project. Documentation and code organization are continuously being improved.

---

## Overview

This repository contains the implementation developed during my undergraduate thesis in Physics Engineering.

The project focuses on stochastic simulation of semiconductor crystal growth using two different atomistic models:

- Solid-on-Solid (SOS)
- Zinc Blende

Additionally, the project evaluates GPU acceleration using Numba CUDA and compares the computational performance against serial implementations.

